<title>UK: Portugal's IGCP plans French franc Eurobond - CDC.</title>
<headline>Portugal's IGCP plans French franc Eurobond - CDC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Institute for Public Credit Management (IGCP) plans to launch a French franc Eurobond, joint lead manager CDC Marche said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The issue is expected to have a 10-year maturity. Other terms were not available.</p>
<p>Banque Nationale de Paris and Lehman Brothers are also joint lead managers of the deal.</p>
<p>The IGCP borrows on behalf of Republic of Portugal, CDC Marche said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
